# Chat kickoff — `<MARKER>`

Generated by `/onboard` step 8. Read this once, then paste the kickoff block at the bottom into your Claude.ai project.

## 1. Create the Claude.ai project

1. Open https://claude.ai and click **Create project** (top-left, "+ New project").
2. Name it whatever you like — `<MARKER>` works.
3. In **Project knowledge**, attach `docs/onboarding/chat-instructions.md` from this repo (upload the file, or paste its contents).
4. In **Settings → Connectors**, attach:
   - **Linear** (workspace-scoped — the same workspace whose API key you put in `.env`)
   - **GitHub** (repo read access for `<REPO_URL>`)

Both connectors must be at the **project level**, not the workspace level — otherwise chat-Claude can't see them inside the project.

## 2. Paste the kickoff message

Open the project chat and paste the block below verbatim. It primes chat-Claude with everything it needs to resume `/discovery` from where `/onboard` left off.

```
I'm starting a fresh Solo-Setup project.

- Marker: <MARKER>
- Repo: <REPO_URL>
- Linear team: <LINEAR_TEAM_NAME>

My answer to the first north-star question — "What problem does this project solve?" — was:

> <NORTH_STAR_Q1_ANSWER>

Please run /discovery and pick up at Phase 2 (Research) using this as the Phase 1 seed. The Phase 1 idea brief lives in Linear as `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] discovery: idea-brief-v1` — fetch it via the Linear connector before starting.

Persistence convention: every document you produce in this conversation must be written to a Linear document under `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN]`. The repo on GitHub is generated from Linear, not the other way around. Do not write to local files.
```

## 3. What happens next

Chat-Claude runs `/discovery` Phase 2 (Research) → Phase 3 (Challenge) → Phase 4 (Improve/Loop) → Phase 5 (Exit). On approve exit, it Task-invokes `/constitution` (seed mode) and writes `docs/product/north-star.md` plus a framing ticket — all via Linear.

When the constitution is seeded, you're ready to run `/specify` against the framing ticket. That happens back in Claude Code, not chat.

## Notes

- **Why the split?** Discovery is multi-day, conversational, and benefits from chat-Claude's UI (web search, longer-context reasoning). Build is structured, file-touching, and belongs in Claude Code.
- **State source-of-truth is Linear.** Both surfaces read the same documents, so you can resume `/discovery` from either side at any time.
- **`<LINEAR_TEAM_NAME>` is the Linear team the kickoff message references.** If you share a team with another marker, ticket IDs in Linear's UI will show that team's key prefix (e.g. `SOL-47`) even for `<MARKER>` work — see `.claude/rules/naming.md` §Shared Linear teams.
